This took me a while to figure out, too.  You a)pply the magic marker.  You
will be asked what you want to write on and given a list of your spells (hint,
hint :-) to choose from.  If you choose a scroll of blank paper (This scroll
appears to be blank...No, wait...) you will be asked what to write.

Here you write *just* the name of the scroll, i.e. not 'scroll of' as well.
So if you want a scroll of enchant armor:

What do you want to write? enchant armor

Note that you can only make spells you've identified otherwise you write some-
thing silly and destroy the scroll fo blank paper.

This could be pretty powerful.  Perhaps it should take mana or something away
to do this (I mean a *lot*) to make it somewhat costly to do.  Actually,
maybe it does take mana, I never noticed.

